{
 "about": "Naming rules for places in the game map. 'required' lists every place name the game code looks up by its exact text (collected from src/ when the reconstruction was made); the build fails if one goes missing, so a rename here never silently breaks a race, mission, event or hall. 'rename' corrects source spellings. 'exclude' drops candidate places that are not real point destinations. 'kind' overrides a place's map category. 'pin' fixes the disambiguated name of a place the game references to its source feature id, so a newly mapped neighbour cannot rename it. 'Vikings Hostel' is renamed 'Mensah Sarbah Vikings Hostel' (owner) to tell it apart from Mensah Sarbah Hall (nicknamed Vikings) and its annexes. Pentagon (owner): the new blocks are 'New Pent Block A/B/C'; the Old Pent courts west to east are Dar es Salaam, Kampala, the admin block, Addis Ababa and Nairobi (the source names had them in a different order); 'Pent Hostel Block A' was a duplicate point of New Pent Block A.",
